error[E0469]: `as` can lose information: `T` to `f64`
  --> tests/programs/numbers/conversions/e0469.la:1:32
  |
1 | fun widen<T: Num>(x: T): f64 = x as f64;
  |                                ^^^^^^^^
  |
  = help: name the conversion, which works at every instance: `x.saturate<f64>()`, `x.round<f64>()` or `x.try_into<f64>()`

error[E0469]: `as` can lose information: `i64` to `u8`
  --> tests/programs/numbers/conversions/e0469.la:5:13
  |
5 |     let a = big as u8;
  |             ^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = help: `x.truncate<u8>()` keeps the low bits; `x.saturate<u8>()` clamps to the range; `x.try_into<u8>()` gives an `Option`

error[E0469]: `as` can lose information: `f64` to `i64`
  --> tests/programs/numbers/conversions/e0469.la:6:13
  |
6 |     let b = 2.5 as i64;
  |             ^^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = help: `x.round<i64>()`, `x.floor<i64>()` and `x.ceil<i64>()` round and panic out of range; `x.saturate<i64>()` rounds toward zero and clamps; `x.try_into<i64>()` gives an `Option`

error[E0469]: `as` can lose information: `i64` to `f64`
  --> tests/programs/numbers/conversions/e0469.la:7:13
  |
7 |     let c = big as f64;
  |             ^^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = help: `x.round<f64>()` gives the nearest `f64`; `x.try_into<f64>()` gives an `Option`, `None` unless it is exact

error[E0469]: `as` can lose information: `u32` to `char`
  --> tests/programs/numbers/conversions/e0469.la:9:13
  |
9 |     let d = n as char;
  |             ^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = help: `x.try_into<char>()` gives an `Option`, `None` unless `x` is a valid code point

error[E0469]: `as` can lose information: `char` to `u8`
   --> tests/programs/numbers/conversions/e0469.la:10:13
   |
10 |     let e = 'é' as u8;
   |             ^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: convert the code point: `(c as u32).truncate<u8>()` or `(c as u32).try_into<u8>()`

For more about E0469, run `lughac explain E0469`.
